{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For the name of HaShem I call.</b> Behold, the one who prays calls the name of HaShem, as it says: קָרָאתִי שִׁמְךָ ה׳ מִבּוֹר תַּחְתִּיּוֹת (Lamentations 3:55), and likewise וּשְׁמוּאֵל בְּקֹרְאֵי שְׁמוֹ, קֹרְאִים אֶל ה׳ וְהוּא יַעֲנֵם (Psalms 99:6). He says: if so, when I pray for the ingathering of exiles, saying כְּנֶשֶׁר יָעִיר קִנּוֹ (Deuteronomy 32:11), and for the coming of the Messiah, saying ה׳ בָּדָד יַנְחֶנּוּ (Deuteronomy 32:12), and at the end of the song, saying הַרְנִינוּ גוֹיִם עַמּוֹ (Deuteronomy 32:43) — you who have known His greatness through the intelligible wonders set forth in His Torah <sup>[end of comment]</sup>" "<b>Ascribe greatness to our Elohim.</b> Do not ascribe to Him any change on account of what is recounted in the song concerning the things that will befall Israel, and that He will turn to become your enemy — for you have known through the wonders of His Torah that He is."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:56.617865464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}